WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.981
Review sheet.

2
00:00:01.261 --> 00:00:08.899
A derivative can be estimated by nudging; the central difference is accurate to order h squared and is your independent check.

3
00:00:09.179 --> 00:00:20.208
A computation is a DAG of elementary operations, each knowing only its local derivatives: add routes, multiply swaps, tanh uses 1 minus t squared.

4
00:00:20.488 --> 00:00:27.976
The chain rule sums over paths, so gradients accumulate, and nodes must be processed in reverse topological order.

5
00:00:28.256 --> 00:00:35.979
Reverse mode gets the gradient of one output with respect to all inputs in one pass, at the cost of storing the forward pass.

6
00:00:36.259 --> 00:00:40.696
Next lesson: build neurons and a network on top of your engine, and train it.
